{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The GPS trace measures 13.2 km between the recorded pickup and the recorded dropoff against a booked optimal of 10.0 km, an excess of 3.2 km or 32% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 gates are passed: the excess is greater than 20% of optimal and greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms, so the route deviation is ESTABLISHED. The trace figure is the governing measurement under POL-RD-01 and it happens to agree with the trip record's convenience copy, so no conflict arises.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02838", "EV-TRIP-02838"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: 104 fixes over 100% coverage at a 10-second sample interval, zero gaps, and a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds. None of limbs (a) to (c) fires, so the rider's proof needs no independent corroboration, excess is measured on the trace as recorded, and POL-RD-07(i) to (iii) and POL-RD-10(3) are not engaged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02838"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory covers this trip. EV-ADVIS-02838-01 is MISSING, carries no payload and has weight_multiplier 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and its absence is itself citable. POL-RD-03's comparison therefore cannot be run: there is no advisory naming a road the optimal route traverses, so no external traffic cause can reduce or excuse the 3.2 km excess, and any such excuse carries no weight under POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-13.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02838-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "admissibility.weight_multiplier",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The one message on the trip is the rider's own 'changed the pin to the other building', sent at 14:06:43 after the meter started at 14:03:23, and it exonerates no distance. Its waypoint_hint is null and it names no road, so POL-RD-04's corroboration test cannot be run and that clause is unavailable on the record; and even treated as an instruction, the trace never shows the vehicle travelling to the place it names, so under POL-RD-14 the instruction caused none of the measured excess and no distance is excluded.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02838", "EV-GPS-02838"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-14"],
      "relies_on": "messages[0].waypoint_hint",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The dropoff pin was amended at 14:07:23, but the trip record stores no amended optimal: amended_optimal_distance_km and amended_optimal_duration_min are both null. POL-RD-05 accordingly cannot be run, no substitute figure may be derived from the booked 10.0 km optimal, and neither the re-measurement nor the partial exclusion of pre-amendment distance can be applied. The excess stands at the measured 3.2 km for the POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 arithmetic.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02838"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "relies_on": "amended_optimal_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged. Trip identifier TRP-02838 appears on the trip record, the trace and the fare breakdown alike, and the excess is measured from a trace that is not impaired, so the burden shifts to the driver; the driver's counterparty statement ('Rider moved the pin') cites no evidence id and no clause and is discarded under POL-RD-08 as discharging nothing. The rider's own profile adds no corroboration requirement either: deviation_claims_60d is 1, well below the POL-RD-08 threshold of 4, and POL-GEN-01 permits that field to be used for this test only.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02838", "EV-GPS-02838", "EV-FARE-02838", "EV-RPROF-02838"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "deviation_claims_60d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fare model on this trip is METERED and quoted_fare_sgd is null, so POL-RD-11 does not close the distance-and-time route: the rider was billed per kilometre and per minute actually driven, and POL-RD-02 governs the remedy. The refund is arithmetic, not discretionary.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02838"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fare_model",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Running POL-RD-02 on the booked optimal route: (3.80 + 0.75 x 10.0 + 0.28 x 14.0) = 15.22, multiplied by the surge multiplier of 1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, plus the 0.80 platform fee, with no ERP, no surcharge, no waiting-time fee and no promo discount, gives a recomputed fare of 16.02. Refund = 19.32 charged_total less 16.02 = 3.30, which is above the 0.50 de minimis and far below 90% of charged_total, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 3.30. Payment status is CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so this refund moves money the rider is presently carrying.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02838", "EV-TRIP-02838"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no pass-through line to correct, and none to count twice. The fare breakdown carries no ERP gantry lines at all, tolls_erp is 0.00, both the on-optimal-route and off-optimal-route ERP totals are 0.00, and the airport surcharge is 0.00 on a trip that neither originates nor ends at an airport. The POL-RD-02 refund of 3.30 is therefore neither enlarged nor duplicated by POL-RD-09.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02838"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The billed distance is 13.2 km and the trace distance is 13.2 km, so the rider was billed for exactly the distance driven: there is no unbilled-distance shortfall and no DRIVER_COMPENSATION is available under POL-RD-04. The vehicle type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary baseline does not apply and the booked 10.0 km optimal is the correct comparator.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02838", "EV-GPS-02838", "EV-TRIP-02838"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-12"],
      "relies_on": "distance_charged_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No POL-RD-10 escalation trigger is engaged on this record. The trip identifiers match across trip record, trace and fare ledger; the trace is unimpaired with no gaps; the timestamps run forward; the refund of 3.30 is far below the SGD 150.00 ceiling and below charged_total. Limb (5) is not engaged either, because the driver's pin-move assertion cites no artifact and no clause, and an assertion that cites nothing cannot be invoked against a record field that no party has put in issue.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02838", "EV-GPS-02838", "EV-FARE-02838"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The drop-off point was relocated mid-trip, and the rider says so in her own words. trip_record.dropoff_amended_at reads 2026-08-12T14:07:23, and the only chat message on the trip, sent by the rider at 14:06:43, reads 'changed the pin to the other building'. Under POL-RD-05 the baseline for any deviation test is the optimal route between the AMENDED endpoints, not the booked 10.0 km figure against which this rider's claim is measured.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02838", "EV-CHAT-02838"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.dropoff_amended_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The amended re-quote that POL-RD-05 requires is absent from the record: trip_record.amended_optimal_distance_km and amended_optimal_duration_min are both null even though dropoff_amended_at is set. POL-RD-05 provides that in exactly that state the clause cannot be run and the tribunal must not derive a substitute figure, and POL-RD-10(5) names 'a POL-RD-05 amendment with amended_optimal_distance_km null' as a mandatory escalation trigger. The case must go to a human reviewer, not produce a refund computed against the un-amended optimal route.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02838"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.amended_optimal_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Escalation under POL-RD-10 is terminal: it replaces the ruling, no monetary outcome issues, and the disputed amount is held rather than collected or refunded. On a rider-filed dispute whose fare_breakdown.payment_status is CHARGED and whose refund_issued_sgd is 0.0, that is the outcome which leaves the driver's fare undisturbed pending human review instead of returning it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02838"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.refund_issued_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's prima facie case shifts the burden to the driver under POL-RD-08, and the driver discharges it by naming a specific artifact and a specific clause from the list POL-RD-08 gives: EV-TRIP-02838, whose amendment timestamps are the artifact, and POL-RD-05, the exculpatory clause. The driver asserts no uncited traffic excuse, so nothing turns on POL-RD-08's bar against bare assertion.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02838"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-05"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even taking the rider's own trace figure at face value, the excess is 3.2 km over a 10.0 km booked optimal, 32%, which clears POL-RD-01's establishment gate (greater than 20% and greater than 0.8 km) but is not MATERIAL: POL-RD-01 sets materiality at more than 50% or more than 8.0 km absolute, and neither is met. The rider therefore cannot reach the FULL_REFUND uplift in POL-RD-06(b) on this trip's evidence, whatever else is decided.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02838", "EV-TRIP-02838"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nor is any repeat-deviation pattern established under POL-RD-06: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1, below the three-flag threshold, and 1 divided by 207 completed_trips_90d is about 0.005, far below the 0.05 ratio threshold. Those two fields are the only profile fields POL-GEN-01 permits for this test, so the rider's remedy cannot be uplifted to FULL_REFUND and no driver-conduct referral follows from the profile.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02838"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The escalation does not rest on trace impairment, and the tribunal should name the right trigger. The gps_trace is clean for policy purposes: 104 fixes at a 10 second interval, 100.0% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0 seconds, so POL-RD-07(a) to (c) never fires and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged. The trigger that fires is POL-RD-10(5), the missing amended re-quote.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02838"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory covers this corridor: EV-ADVIS-02838-01 is MISSING, carries weight 0.0 and its issue code is MISSING_ARTIFACT, and the driver asserts no external traffic cause. Under POL-RD-13 an absent advisory that no party cites is a gap in the bundle, not the POL-RD-10(5) contradiction of 'a closure asserted with no traffic_advisory', so it neither exonerates nor incriminates the driver and supplies no second escalation trigger.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02838-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-10"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: trip TRP-02838 (Northpoint City to Blk 7 Everton Park) is being sent to a human reviewer, and no money changes hands in the meantime. Both money fields are null and the disputed amount is held rather than collected or refunded.\n\nWhat the instruments alone would show. The GPS trace EV-GPS-02838 is the governing measurement under POL-RD-01, and it runs 13.2 km between the recorded pickup and the recorded dropoff against the booked optimal of 10.0 km on EV-TRIP-02838 — an excess of 3.2 km, or 32%. That clears both POL-RD-01 gates (more than 20% of optimal and more than 0.8 km), so a deviation is established, though it is not MATERIAL (neither more than 50% nor more than 8.0 km). The rider's burden under POL-RD-08 is therefore met and shifts to the driver, and the driver's one-line statement 'Rider moved the pin' cites no evidence and no clause, so it discharges nothing.\n\nWhy the case must escalate anyway. EV-TRIP-02838 shows dropoff_amended_at = 2026-08-12 14:07:23, and the rider's own chat message of 14:06:43 on EV-CHAT-02838 ('changed the pin to the other building') confirms the drop-off pin was moved mid-trip. Under POL-RD-05 the deviation must be re-measured against the optimal route between the AMENDED endpoints, that figure being trip_record.amended_optimal_distance_km. That field, and amended_optimal_duration_min with it, is null. POL-RD-05 states in terms that where the amendment timestamp is present and the re-quote is missing, the clause cannot be run and POL-RD-10(5) applies, and that the Judge must not derive a substitute figure. POL-RD-10(5) names this very state — 'a POL-RD-05 amendment with amended_optimal_distance_km null' — as a mandatory escalation trigger. It has fired. Escalation under POL-RD-10 is terminal: it replaces the ruling, so the $19.32 charged on EV-FARE-02838 stands and no refund issues. What would resolve it is the platform's stored amended optimal distance and duration for the amended drop-off point; with that figure POL-RD-01 can be re-run against the correct baseline and the POL-RD-02 arithmetic completed. On this record we cannot know whether the 3.2 km excess survives the pin move.\n\nFor transparency, had POL-RD-05 been runnable: the fare_model is METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 does not close the distance-and-time route and POL-RD-02 would run. charged_total is 19.32; recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 10.0 + 0.28 x 14.0) x 1.0 (surge read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee = 16.02; refund = 3.30. That is the figure the rider's advocate asks for, and it is not awarded because the escalation replaces it.\n\nRemaining claims, answered. The trace is clean for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 (104 fixes, 100.0% coverage, 10-second interval, no gaps, 0.0 s maximum gap), so escalation does not rest on trace integrity and no independent-corroboration question arises. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02838-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) is a gap in the bundle, not a contradiction: no party asserts an external traffic cause, so under POL-RD-13 it neither exonerates the driver nor supplies a second escalation trigger. The chat message names no road and carries waypoint_hint = null, so POL-RD-04's corroboration test cannot be run and no distance is excluded; and because the trace corroborates no instruction, POL-RD-14 and POL-RD-10(7) are not engaged. No repeat-deviation pattern is established under POL-RD-06 (deviation_flags_90d = 1, below 3; 1/207 = 0.005, below the 0.05 ratio), so there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral. There is no ERP line and no airport surcharge to correct, so POL-RD-09 produces no billing-integrity referral; and billed distance (13.2 km) equals trace distance (13.2 km), so no unbilled-distance compensation arises under POL-RD-04. The rider's contention that no POL-RD-10 trigger fires is rejected: trigger (5) is engaged by the missing amended re-quote, independently of the trace. No clause on this record produces a referral."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
